.TH LIBTLS_TLS_GET_FD 3 "2023-04-01" "libtls" "TLS Library"
.SH NAME
tls_get_fd - Get TLS file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <libtls.h>
.sp
.B fd_type
.B tls_get_fd(tls_t* tls);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B tls_get_fd
function returns the file descriptor associated with a TLS instance.
The
.B tls
argument is a pointer to the TLS instance.
The function returns the file descriptor, or 0 if the TLS instance is not associated with a file descriptor.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B tls_get_fd
function to get the file descriptor associated with a TLS instance:
.nf
.B #include <libtls.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.sp
.B int main() {
.B   tls_t* tls = ...; // Assume a valid TLS instance
.B   fd_type fd = tls_get_fd(tls);
.B   if(fd == 0) {
.B     fprintf(stderr, "Error getting TLS file descriptor\n");
.B     return 1;
.B   }

.B   // Use the file descriptor

.B   return 0;
.B }
.ne
.fi
